<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African July trade surplus 2.58 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African July trade surplus 2.58 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa recorded a trade surplus of 2.58 billion rand in July from a 27.6 million rand deficit in June, latest South African Revenue Service figures show.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast an average 600 million rand surplus.  </p>
<p>(Data in billions of rand - rounded)</p>
<p>			Jul '96		Jun '96	    Jul '95</p>
<p>Exports	     13.72		   8.84		9.41</p>
<p>Imports	     11.14		   8.87		9.09</p>
<p>Balance		2.58		  -0.03		0.32</p>
<p>			Jan-Jul '96	 Jan-Jul '95</p>
<p>Exports	     67.66		  58.25</p>
<p>Imports	     64.19		  56.42</p>
<p>Balance		3.46		   1.83</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
</text>
